      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "Use this initializer to create rules at positions along two axes, and a range along a third axis:",
      "normalizedSource": "Use this initializer to create rules at positions along two axes, and a range along a third axis:",
      "sourceHash": "d6b7cb16174694f83c3ba97f7dbefa2a5117ab6ee60dbeab25cd48ccb9367a70",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "❗ **Important**: A 3D RuleMark requires exactly two numeric points and one numeric range.",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\nChart3D {\n    // A red rule from from -0.5 to 0.5 on the x-axis, positioned at y = 0, z = 0\n    RuleMark(\n        x: .value(\"x\", -0.5..<0.5),\n        y: .value(\"y\", 0),\n        z: .value(\"z\", 0)\n    )\n    .foregroundStyle(.red)\n\n    // A green rule from -0.5 to 0.5 on the y-axis, positioned at x = 0, z = 0\n    RuleMark(\n        x: .value(\"x\", 0),\n        y: .value(\"y\", -0.5..<0.5),\n        z: .value(\"z\", 0)\n    )\n    .foregroundStyle(.green)\n\n    // A blue rule from from -0.5 to 0.5 on the z-axis, positioned at x = 0, y = 0\n    RuleMark(\n        x: .value(\"x\", 0),\n        y: .value(\"y\", 0),\n        z: .value(\"z\", -0.5..<0.5)\n    )\n    .foregroundStyle(.blue)\n}\n```",
      "documentTitle": "init(x:y:z:)",
      "framework": "Charts",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
